  "notes": "USAGE:\nCovers a range from innocent doodling (in notebooks) to vandalism (on buildings and public property). The tone depends on context — a child's doodle is harmless, while graffiti on cultural heritage sites is a serious issue.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {落書|らくが}きをする: to scribble, to doodle, to graffiti\n- {落書|らくが}きを{消|け}す: to remove graffiti\n- {落書|らくが}き{帳|ちょう}: sketchbook, doodle pad",
